## 5. Risks and Mitigations
| Risk ID | Description | Impact | Likelihood | Severity | Mitigation Action | Owner |
|---------|-------------|--------|------------|----------|-------------------|-------|
| R1      | Dynamic Jira API token expiry or revocation | High   | Medium     | High     | Implement token refresh logic and monitor expiry; use test accounts with stable permissions | QA Lead |
| R2      | Unstable network connectivity to Jira cloud | Medium | Medium     | Medium   | Use tcconfig to simulate and test network drops; retry logic in test scripts | QA Lead |
| R3      | Mock/stub service not matching live Jira error payloads | Medium | Low        | Medium   | Align mock responses with Jira API schema; validate against live errors | Test Architect |
| R4      | SLA breach in authentication response times | Medium | Low        | Medium   | Use JMeter to simulate load and monitor SLA; alert on threshold breach | Performance QA |
| R5      | Unauthorized access not surfaced clearly in logs | Medium | Low        | Medium   | Ensure error logging is enabled and validated in all environments | DevOps |

---

## 6. Test Schedule / Milestones
- Test design: 2 days
- Script development: 3 days
- Environment setup: 1 day
- Execution: 2 days
- Reporting & closure: 1 day
- Total duration: 1 week
- Resources: 1 QA Lead, 1 Test Architect, 1 Automation Engineer

